today the council gave its assessment to  the work done on the field of transport  under the Estonian presidency back in  June with the Commission presented its  first mobility package the biggest  transport initiative of the Unocal  Commission the council recognized that  significant progress has been made with  regulating access to market we have also  moved closer to the range agreement on  the more harmonized European market for  hire vehicles  there have been important steps forward  on driving and rest time rules of the  drivers transport is about people and  today we discussed the number of points  of interest for EU citizens and new  workers first the Commission's proposal  to improve the functioning of a road  toiler market and improve social and  employment conditions second point the  future of road charging in Europe in May  we proposed to modernize row charging to  better tackle the external cost of road  transport today we had a debate which  showed that many member states support  the idea of smart road charging the  council took stock of the progress made  on the proposal on safeguarding  competition in air transport and it aims  to ensure fair competition between new  airlines and third country carriers  while maintaining a high level of air  connectivity throughout europe finally I  would like to underline that the Council  adopted three sets of conclusions first  on the digital transport second on the  implementation of 20 network and the  safe instrument and third on the midterm  review of Galileo and EGNOS these three  conclusions set a forward-looking vision  for the innovative competitive and  multimodal transport system for Europe
 

